From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:13:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(world): synchronize jukebox occupancy and playback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bedrock sends disc sounds by name, while Java uses a jukebox level event keyed by the sent song registry. Forward the named sound through that event so playback, stopping, and nearby entity reactions share Java’s jukebox lifecycle. Stop playback when a jukebox block is removed, including when Bedrock does not send a separate stop sound.
